%% plays.glp --- the GSG mini-app activated as the super-app activates it (GSG paper, Section 2, "Activation and joining"): by run/3, under the type identity of its entry miniapp/4, with its grants; and, for two executions, with the two ends of one root channel handed to them as their conversation, the play standing in for the social graph, as the village of programs/currencies/coins does.  The certified mini-app is this program, whose module value self_module/1 gives; the persons are scripted (person.glp), each under its role, and each play returns their screens.  A run does not end --- the agent's request question stays open and the person channel never closes --- so once each agent has taken its own transactions until none holds and no trigger is left, the run suspends, and a play's result is read off a partial stream.  The super-app hosting the mini-app on two smartphones is ../gsg_boot.glp.

imported procedure person#miniapp_person(Key?, Constant?, Channel(PersonOut(Drawn), PersonIn(Drawn))?, Stream(Seen)).
imported procedure miniapp#router(Stream(NetEvent)?, Routes?, List(Net)?, Stream(Net)).

%% play_friends(A, B): alice and bob, one conversation between their two executions.  Each asks to know the other, and each agent sends the other a hello on the conversation; once alice knows bob she offers him friendship, his approval question asks him, and he answers yes (GSG:1, Friendship, an act of both); once it commits bob ends the friendship, which asks nobody (GSG:2, Ending a friendship, an act of one).
exported procedure play_friends(Stream(Seen), Stream(Seen)).
play_friends(A?, B?) :-
    self_module(M),
    find_type(miniapp/4, T),
    run(miniapp(alice, ch(GA?, DA), ch([conversation(bob, ch(BA?, AB))], _), []), T?, M?),
    person # miniapp_person(alice, alice, ch(DA?, GA), A),
    run(miniapp(bob, ch(GB?, DB), ch([conversation(alice, ch(AB?, BA))], _), []), T?, M?),
    person # miniapp_person(bob, bob, ch(DB?, GB), B).

%% play_held(In, ToBob, ToCarol): the router of alice's mini-app, on what it reads in this order: a hello to bob and a hello to carol, sent before any conversation is open, and so held; the conversation with bob, which carries bob's hello in and the hello held for him out, carol's still held; a start to bob, on his conversation; and the conversation with carol, which carries the hello held for her.  The events end, and the router closes the conversations' outgoing streams. Expected: In = [msg(alice, hello(bob))],
%%   ToBob = [msg(bob, hello(alice)), msg(bob, cargo(alice, start(attempt(alice,
%%   1, 1, befriend(alice, bob)))))], ToCarol = [msg(carol, hello(alice))].
exported procedure play_held(Stream(Net), Stream(Net), Stream(Net)).
play_held(In?, ToBob?, ToCarol?) :-
    miniapp # router([sent(msg(bob, hello(alice))),
                      sent(msg(carol, hello(alice))),
                      opened(bob, ch([msg(alice, hello(bob))], ToBob)),
                      sent(msg(bob, cargo(alice, start(attempt(alice, 1, 1, befriend(alice, bob)))))),
                      opened(carol, ch([], ToCarol))],
                     [], [], In).
